README for the MEX interace for the UAL

1. Working principles

The basic principle of MEX files will not be discussed here, refer to the MATLAB documentation for more information on MEX files.

The code generation of methods for IDSs has been adapted from the one developed for the CPP interface and is therefore very similar, including the dedicated functions for treating each field of type structure or array of structures.

Since MATLAB uses column-major order for arrays (i.e. as in FORTRAN), no re-ordering of the data in arrays is necessary. However trailing singleton dimensions are never shown for multi-dimensional arrays (at least 3-dimensional), hence ones have to be added if needed when dealing with this type of arrays.


2. Notes

   - To accomodate compatibility with the present MATLAB interface options have been implemented to convert fields of type INT to double value and to replace NaN values by EMPTY_FLOAT both in get and put methods.

   - Treatment of strings requires casting from the intrinsic char type in C (8 bits) and the mxChar type used in MATLAB character arrays (16 bits). Additionally, string vectors (STR_1D) are represented using cell array of strings which differs from the AL lowlevel representation using char matrices.

3. List of functions

The standard functions have been implemented:
    - Functions to open/create/close a pulse file
        + imas_open_env
        + imas_open_public
        + imas_create_env
        + imas_create_public
        + imas_close
    - Function to query the backend in use
        + imas_get_backendID
    - Functions to read/write IDSs
        + ids_delete
        + ids_get
        + ids_get_slice
        + ids_put
        + ids_put_slice
    - Function to initialize an IDS structure
        + ids_gen

The following additional functions are also provided
    - Functions to open/create/close a pulse file (requires fiddling with the environment)
        + imas_open
        + imas_create
    - Functions to query/modify the global parameters for the MEX interface (see 4.)
        + imas_get_mex_params
        + imas_set_mex_params
    - Converters
        + ids_int_to_double
        + ids_double_to_int
        + ids_empty_to_nan
        + ids_nan_to_empty
        + ids_cell_to_struct
        + ids_struct_to_cell
    - Functions to initialize an IDS structure
        + ids_gen2            (provides empty arrays of structures, whereas ids_gen provides scalar arrays of structures)
        + ids_allocate        (for allocating arrays of structures)
    - Function to generate an IDS structure with random field values (for tests only)
        + ids_rand

4. Parameters

List of current valid parameters:
    - get_int_as_double                         (default:0)
        In get methods, convert integer fields to double.
    - put_int_from_double                       (default:1)
        In put methods, allows to provide double values for integer fields.
    - get_empty_as_nan                          (default:0)
        In get methods, for fields of type float replace EMPTY_FLOAT values by NaNs.
    - put_empty_from_nan                        (default:0)
        In put methods, for fields of type float replace NaNs by EMPTY_FLOAT.
    - use_cell_array_for_array_of_structures    (default:1)
        If enabled arrays of structures will be represented using cell arrays of structes (default), otherwise using structure arrays.
    - convert_whole_ids                         (default:0)
        If disabled the conversions (int <-> double) and (EMPTY_FLOAT <-> NaN) will be performed just before/after  calling the lowlevel write/read routines, otherwise they will be performed in one block.
    - error_on_missing_field                    (default:1)
        If enabled put methods will trigger an error if any field is missing from the input IDS.
    - verbosity                                 (default:0)
        Controls the verbosity level of the interface, higher means more verbose. Minimum value is 0, maximum value is 4.

